  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enabling Access to Internally Displaced Populations and Migrants to COVID-19 Vaccination in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to the national COVID-19 vaccination strategy ensuring migrants, international travelers, border users, frontline workers at the border, local and vulnerable communities living along the border have access to quality COVID-19 immunization services. The project will target seven priority points of entry (PoE) in four provinces and focus on training of frontline health workers, development and dissemination of COVID-19 risk communication messages for travelers and border users and implementation of the COVID-19 vaccination at the PoE.</narrative>
  </description>
